        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does Georgia pollen or humidity damage the glass or hardware?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Spring pollen leaves a yellow film on everything in Georgia, glass included, and it rinses off with a hose in minutes. Humidity does not affect tempered 12 mm glass, and the spigots are 2205 marine-grade stainless steel with a 10-year no-rust promise. There are no pickets to scrub and no wood to stain every couple of years.</p>",
            "pages": ""
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use the railing on a mountain cabin deck that gets snow?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Tempered glass and stainless spigots do not absorb water, so freeze-thaw in Blue Ridge or Blairsville does not crack or swell them. The deck framing carries any snow load; the railing only needs a sound attachment to the joists with the blocking shown in the installation guide. The side-mount spigot works on a fascia board when the deck boards are too thin.</p>",
            "pages": ""
          }
        },
