        "t1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>What Georgia homeowners build with glass</strong></p><p>Metro Atlanta is the center of it. Intown bungalows in Morningside, Virginia-Highland and Decatur sit on sloped lots with tall back decks. A glass deck railing keeps the yard in view. Buckhead and Midtown add condo balconies, while Alpharetta, Roswell and Marietta bring pool decks and open staircases. See the <a href=\"/pages/georgia-glass-railing-atlanta\">glass railings in Atlanta</a> page for that market.</p><p>North of the city, Lake Lanier homes around Cumming, Buford and Gainesville stack decks toward the water. Lake Oconee, between Atlanta and Augusta, has a similar mix of lake houses and golf lots. In the North Georgia mountains, cabins in Blue Ridge, Ellijay, Blairsville and Big Canoe have view decks facing the ridges, where glass beats pickets. On the coast, Savannah, Tybee Island, St. Simons and Sea Island combine salt air with raised houses and porches. Augusta, Athens and Macon round out the state.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Georgia code in short</strong></p><p>Georgia sets its building rules through the Georgia State Minimum Standard Codes. The current editions are the 2018 International Residential Code and International Building Code, with Georgia amendments. The Georgia code sets guards at 36 inches minimum for houses and 42 inches for commercial and multifamily buildings, including condo balconies. For pools, Georgia applies the 2018 International Swimming Pool and Spa Code, and section 305 sets a 48-inch barrier. Our 46-inch panel in spigots gives that height.</p><p>Permits are issued locally, by a city office such as the City of Atlanta Office of Buildings or by the county. Check with your local building department about whether a railing replacement or a new deck needs a permit. Our engineering documents, with testing results and blocking details for wood and concrete, are available for the permit file. The full summary is on our <a href=\"/pages/georgia-building-code-for-glass-railing\">Georgia building code for glass railing</a> page.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Delivery to any Georgia address</strong></p><p>Orders ship from our warehouse in Quebec and cross the border before they reach you. The price at checkout is final, with no duties, tariffs or brokerage charges later. Standard orders are processed in 2 to 3 business days, then delivered by freight carrier in 5 to 10 business days. The truck has a liftgate, so the crate comes down to the driveway. That works on a mountain road in Ellijay or a cul-de-sac in Johns Creek. Custom glass takes 2 to 3 weeks of shipping after processing.</p><p>Orders over 3,000 USD ship free; the <a href=\"/pages/free-shipping-information\">free shipping page</a> has the details. Open the crate on arrival and report any damage within 3 days, before installation. We replace or refund the damaged item at no cost.</p>"
          }
        }
